    "---\n",
    "# 2. Python basics\n",
    "\n",
    "## Syntax (slide 8)\n",
    "In Python, code is written with indentation instead of brackets.\n",
    "Compared to C++ or Java, variables do not need to be initialized with a certain type.\n",
    "\n",
    "| C++ | Java |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| <pre>int x=4;<br>int y=7;<br>if (x > y){<br>std::cout << \"x bigger than y\";<br>}</pre> | <pre>int x=4;<br>int y=7;<br>if (x > y){<br>System.out.println(\"x bigger than y\");<br>}</pre> |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a271556b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 8 – Python\n",
    "x = 4\n",
    "y = 7\n",
    "if x > y:\n",
    "    print(\"x bigger than y\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76417676",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "❓ **Why is there no output?** `4 > 7` is `False`, so the indented block is skipped.\n",
    "Try changing `x` to `10` and run the cell again."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bf92a1c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Functions (slide 9)\n",
    "A function is declared with `def`. It can take input values and return values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f38efa8f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 9 – Example function\n",
    "def add(a, b):\n",
    "    result = a + b\n",
    "    return result"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "36f58515",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Calling a function (slide 10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "aebb859f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 10 – Passing variables\n",
    "num1 = 3\n",
    "num2 = 5\n",
    "sum = add(num1 , num2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f43429a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra: show the result\n",
    "print(\"sum  =\", sum)\n",
    "print(\"num1 =\", num1, \"| num2 =\", num2, \" <- not changed\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e3182a6f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 10 – Passing values\n",
    "sum = add(3,5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cf13862b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra\n",
    "print(\"sum =\", sum)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d71d6ac0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Local variables (slide 11)\n",
    "The variables `a`, `b` and `result` inside the function are **not** known outside the function.\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Indentation inside `add` is made consistent here; on the slide the two lines are indented differently, which Python would reject.)*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "70368b8e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 11 – left\n",
    "def add(a,b):\n",
    "    a = a+b\n",
    "    return a\n",
    "\n",
    "a = 3\n",
    "b = 5\n",
    "sum = add(a,b)\n",
    "\n",
    "#Which value will a have now?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d5162bb4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra: reveal\n",
    "print(\"a   =\", a)\n",
    "print(\"sum =\", sum)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9ba6bd2e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 11 – right\n",
    "def add(a,b):\n",
    "    a = a+b\n",
    "    return a\n",
    "\n",
    "a = 3\n",
    "b = 5\n",
    "a = add(a,b)\n",
    "\n",
    "#Which value will a have now?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2fd8a1d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra: reveal\n",
    "print(\"a =\", a)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1a8713d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- **Left:** `a` is 3 because the function uses a **local copy**, not the globally defined variable `a`\n",
    "- **Right:** `a` is 8, it was overwritten with the function's return value"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ec72aee5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ⚠️ Pitfall: we just overwrote the built-in `sum()`!\n",
    "Slides 10 and 11 store the result in a variable called `sum`. That variable hides Python's built-in function `sum()`, which slide 13 needs.\n",
    "Run the next cell to see the problem, then the one after to fix it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3bbca7ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra: demonstrates the problem (this raises a TypeError on purpose)\n",
    "sum([1, 2, 3])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d6de45dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra: remove our variable so the built-in sum() is visible again\n",
    "del sum\n",
    "print(sum([1, 2, 3]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c9b03a42",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Mutable vs. immutable (slide 12)\n",
    "Changes to **immutable** objects in a function are not visible outside it. Changes to **mutable** objects stay visible outside the function.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Mutable types | Immutable types |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Lists, Sets, Dictionaries | Numbers (Integer, Rational, Float, Decimal, Complex & Booleans), Strings, Tuples |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Slide 13"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0c6a9634",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 13 – left: passed list is not changed\n",
    "def sum_values(numbers):\n",
    "    total = sum(numbers)\n",
    "    return total\n",
    "\n",
    "my_numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n",
    "result = sum_values(my_numbers)\n",
    "print(\"Sum of numbers:\", result)\n",
    "# Output: Sum of numbers: 15\n",
    "print(\"Original list:\", my_numbers)\n",
    "# Output: Original list: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fc0f5164",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 13 – right: passed list is changed\n",
    "def sum_and_append(numbers):\n",
    "    total = sum(numbers)\n",
    "    numbers.append(total)\n",
    "    return total\n",
    "\n",
    "my_numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n",
    "result = sum_and_append(my_numbers)\n",
    "print(\"Sum of numbers:\", result)\n",
    "# Output: Sum of numbers: 15\n",
    "print(\"Original list:\", my_numbers)\n",
    "# Output: Original list: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 15]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f596f843",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- **Left:** The passed variable `my_numbers` is not modified\n",
    "- **Right:** The passed variable `my_numbers` is modified with `append`, which adds the calculated sum to the list. The function does **not** work on a local copy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f7af7008",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Classes (slide 14)\n",
    "Classes are defined with `class`. The attributes are set in `__init__()` using `self`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f1c6f8b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 14 – class definition\n",
    "class mammal():\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_legs, fur, diet, territory):\n",
    "        self.num_legs = num_legs\n",
    "        self.fur = fur\n",
    "        self.diet = diet\n",
    "        self.territory = territory"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a443e86f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 14 – many instances with different parameters\n",
    "bear = mammal(4, True, \"Omnivore\", [\"Foest\"])\n",
    "camel = mammal(4, True, \"Herbivore\", [\"Desert\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ea5dd73b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra: look at the two instances\n",
    "print(\"bear :\", bear.num_legs, bear.fur, bear.diet, bear.territory)\n",
    "print(\"camel:\", camel.num_legs, camel.fur, camel.diet, camel.territory)\n",
    "print(vars(bear))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ceac1447",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Inheritance (slide 16)\n",
    "A child class inherits variables and methods from its parent and can add new ones.\n",
    "`bear` inherits from the `mammal` class above (4 parameters, no hunger yet).\n",
    "\n",
    "*(On the slide, the `super(...)` line is shifted out of `__init__`. Here it sits inside `__init__`, where it belongs.)*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ea4c4d97",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 16\n",
    "class bear(mammal):   # This is just pseudo-code to demonstrate the functionality.\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        self.num_legs = 4\n",
    "        self.fur = True\n",
    "        self.diet = \"Omnivore\"\n",
    "        self.territory = [\"Forest\"]\n",
    "        super(bear, self).__init__(self.num_legs, self.fur, self.diet, self.territory)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def roar(self):\n",
    "        self.makes_noise()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a4236957",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra: a bear is created without passing any values\n",
    "b = bear()\n",
    "print(vars(b))\n",
    "print(\"isinstance(b, mammal):\", isinstance(b, mammal))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "775fad3e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`roar()` calls `makes_noise()`, which isn't defined anywhere (pseudo-code), so `b.roar()` would raise an `AttributeError`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5bb63898",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Hunger & methods (slide 15)\n",
    "Methods are functions defined inside a class. They usually work with the class's own variables.\n",
    "Now `mammal` is extended with `hunger` and an `eat()` method."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "75a918c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Slide 15\n",
    "class mammal():   # This is just pseudo-code to demonstrate the functionality.\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_legs, fur, diet, territory, hunger):\n",
    "        self.num_legs = num_legs\n",
    "        self.fur = fur\n",
    "        self.diet = diet\n",
    "        self.territory = territory\n",
    "        self.hunger = hunger\n",
    "\n",
    "    def eat(self, food, food_condition):\n",
    "        if (food_condition is not \"rotten\" and self.is_compatible_with_diet(food)):\n",
    "            self.hunger = 0\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            self.vomit()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7bcd8290",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "💡 Python ≥ 3.8 prints a `SyntaxWarning` for `is not \"rotten\"`: `is` checks whether two names refer to the *same object*, not whether the values are *equal*. Use `!=` to compare values.\n",
    "It is **pseudo-code**: `is_compatible_with_diet()` and `vomit()` don't exist yet, so calling `eat()` fails:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ffcb5ed8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ➕ Extra: try it (raises AttributeError on purpose)\n",
    "m = mammal(4, True, \"Omnivore\", [\"Forest\"], hunger=10)\n",
    "m.eat(\"berries\", \"fresh\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "15c8c5ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Note: the `bear` class above still inherits from the *old* `mammal` (without hunger). Redefining `mammal` does not update classes that were already created from it. The complete version below redefines both."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a691aba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ➕ Extra: the pseudo-code made runnable\n",
    "Same idea as slides 15 + 16, with the missing pieces filled in so we can actually see the methods and the inheritance working."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e8cc0b42",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class mammal():\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_legs, fur, diet, territory, hunger=10):\n",
    "        self.num_legs = num_legs\n",
    "        self.fur = fur\n",
    "        self.diet = diet\n",
    "        self.territory = territory\n",
    "        self.hunger = hunger\n",
    "\n",
    "    def is_compatible_with_diet(self, food):\n",
    "        plants = [\"berries\", \"grass\", \"honey\"]\n",
    "        if self.diet == \"Herbivore\":\n",
    "            return food in plants\n",
    "        if self.diet == \"Carnivore\":\n",
    "            return food not in plants\n",
    "        return True  # Omnivore eats everything\n",
    "\n",
    "    def vomit(self):\n",
    "        print(\"  Bleurgh! 🤢\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def makes_noise(self):\n",
    "        print(\"  *some noise*\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def eat(self, food, food_condition):\n",
    "        print(f\"{type(self).__name__} eats {food_condition} {food} (hunger before: {self.hunger})\")\n",
    "        if food_condition != \"rotten\" and self.is_compatible_with_diet(food):\n",
    "            self.hunger = 0\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            self.vomit()\n",
    "        print(f\"  hunger after: {self.hunger}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class bear(mammal):\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        super(bear, self).__init__(4, True, \"Omnivore\", [\"Forest\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "    def roar(self):\n",
    "        self.makes_noise()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # A child can also override a parent method\n",
    "    def makes_noise(self):\n",
    "        print(\"  ROOOAAAR! 🐻\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "camel = mammal(4, True, \"Herbivore\", [\"Desert\"])\n",
    "teddy = bear()\n",
    "\n",
    "camel.eat(\"grass\", \"fresh\")    # works\n",
    "camel.eat(\"fish\", \"fresh\")     # not compatible with diet\n",
    "teddy.eat(\"fish\", \"rotten\")    # rotten\n",
    "teddy.eat(\"honey\", \"fresh\")    # eat() inherited from mammal\n",
    "teddy.roar()                   # roar() only exists in bear\n",
    "# camel.roar()                 # -> AttributeError: mammal has no roar()\n",
    "print(\"isinstance(teddy, mammal):\", isinstance(teddy, mammal))"
   ]
  },
